diff --git a/docs/1.guide/1.basics/6.error.md b/docs/1.guide/1.basics/6.error.md
index 8bc22d4..591c3e0 100644
--- a/docs/1.guide/1.basics/6.error.md
+++ b/docs/1.guide/1.basics/6.error.md
@@ -75,6 +75,47 @@ This will end the request with `400 - Bad Request` status code and the following
 > [!IMPORTANT]
 > Error `statusText` should be short (max 512 to 1024 characters) and only include tab, spaces or visible ASCII characters and extended characters (byte value 128–255). Prefer `message` in JSON body for extended message.
 
+## Problem Details (RFC 9457)
+
+Use `problem()` to send an [RFC 9457](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457) response (`application/problem+json`). It returns a regular `HTTPError`, so it can be thrown or returned, and only responses created with it change format.
+
+```js
+import { problem } from "h3";
+
+app.get("/users/:id", (event) => {
+  throw problem({
+    status: 404,
+    statusText: "Not Found",
+    message: "User 42 does not exist",
+    type: "https://example.com/errors/not-found",
+    instance: "/users/42",
+    body: { traceId: "abc" },
+  });
+});
+```
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "https://example.com/errors/not-found",
+  "title": "Not Found",
+  "status": 404,
+  "detail": "User 42 does not exist",
+  "instance": "/users/42",
+  "traceId": "abc"
+}
+```
+
+- `statusText` → `title` (defaults to the standard reason phrase of `status`).
+- `message` → `detail` (only when passed explicitly).
+- `body` → extension members at the top level; `data` stays under the `data` key.
+- `type` defaults to `about:blank`; `instance` is only included when set.
+- `type`, `title`, `status`, `detail` and `instance` always win over same-named keys in `body` or `data`.
+- With `unhandled: true`, only `type`, `title` and `status` are sent.
+- A `content-type` set in `headers` is not overridden.
+
+> [!NOTE]
+> Throw `problem()` directly. Wrapping it with `new HTTPError({ cause })` loses the problem format.
+
 ## Unhandled Errors
 
 Any error that occurs during calling [request lifecycle](/guide/basics/lifecycle) without using `HTTPError` will be processed as an _unhandled_ error.
